desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Var In Script Tag"
	title_zh: "检测到Var In Script Tag",
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-var-in-script-tag"
	risk: "xss"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `var-in-script-tag` (/tmp/semgrep-rules/javascript/express/security/audit/xss/pug/var-in-script-tag.yaml).
Original message: Detected a template variable used in a script tag. Although template variables are HTML escaped, HTML escaping does not always prevent cross-site scripting (XSS) attacks when used directly in JavaScript. If you need this data on the rendered page, consider placing it in the HTML portion (outside of a script tag). Alternatively, use a JavaScript-specific encoder, such as the one available in OWASP ESAPI.

CWE: CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')
References:
- https://www.veracode.com/blog/secure-development/nodejs-template-engines-why-default-encoders-are-not-enough
- https://github.com/ESAPI/owasp-esapi-js
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review the flagged code and follow the framework's secure coding guidance: use safe APIs, escape output, and avoid hardcoded credentials.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.pug": <<<POS
script 
 
=OWeYuLbIXW4eo

POS
	"safefile://neg.sample": <<<NEG
# safe sample
no secrets here
just regular code
NEG
)

${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\s*=[A-Za-z0-9]+/) as $p0
${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\s*=.*["']\s*\+.*/) as $p1
${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\s*=[^'"]+\+.*/) as $p2
${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\(.*?\)\s*=\s*[A-Za-z0-9]+/) as $p3
${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\(.*?\)\s*=\s*.*["']\s*\+.*/) as $p4
${*.pug}.pattern_regex(/script\(.*?\)\s*=\s*[^'"]+\+.*/) as $p5
$p0 + $p1 + $p2 + $p3 + $p4 + $p5 as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Var In Script Tag",
	title_zh: "检测到Var In Script Tag",
	message: "Var In Script Tag",
}
